From 3e7519aedbc0d96e1c51461ce703f079a112e413 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 03:42:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dfirst: the star cover of the d loop (--dfirst-star K,
 default 4)

The two diagonals of a magic square of even order share no number, so
for any x* one of them lacks it: the d-first loop may skip the d that
contain x* ("star d") and still find (and flag) every magic square.
msearch picks x* from the whole unreduced list (argmax of the summed
|V_d|^5.5 R^1.4 over the d containing it; 0.04-0.55 s per sum) and
searches every K-th star d (by rank), estimating their pairs K x.

- dfirst.c: dfirst_star_choose, dfirst_set_star, dfirst_star_count, the
  filter and its counts in dfirst_search, a star column in the d log
- msearch: --dfirst-star K (default 4 for even n, off for odd n; -1:
  skip all), --dfirst-star-only; dsum star fields, est_* weighted, two
  strata for se_*
- fuzz_arrange --dfirst: x* against brute force, the filter (K = -1,
  1-5, only, stride splits) against the filtered brute pairs, and planted
  magic pairs with x forced onto one diagonal
- scheduler: complete sums' pairs by est_pairs once per sum
  (dsum_est_pairs), SUMMARY_VERSION 4; test_dfirst_star
- measured star share s = 0.094 / 0.073 / 0.067 / 0.061 at N = 7.6k /
  11.7k / 20.5k / 23k (predicted within 2-4%): K = 4 takes 1.048-1.076x
  less CPU per sum (research/ideas.md, "The star cover of the d loop")

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
